        <rows>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[552]]></id>
                <gid><![CDATA[470]]></gid>
                <group_name><![CDATA[Requirement Rating]]></group_name>
                <description><![CDATA[<p>You will be given several options of Sophist formalization of a requirement. Each option formalizes the requirement in one or multiple Sophist requirements. Rank the different options according to their respective quality (move them via drag and drop). You may put several options into the same box.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.reusecompany.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/SOPHIST-Master-Patterns-Library.pdf">Here</a> you can find a description of the Sophist rules. The Sophist rules may guide your decisions, though this evaluation is not only about the correct usage of the Sophist rules, but about the quality of requirements themselves. Hereby, quality means that the requirements are written to a good standard, that you would write yourself and that they cover the content of the orignial requirements.</p>

<p>The Sophist formalizations are LLM generated. We want to evaluate which configuration produces the best results.</p>

<p>The boxes are of decreasing quality:</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>No update needed:</strong> You would accept the option as the Sophist version of the requirement</li>
	<li><strong>Only small changes necessary:</strong> Within a few seconds, you could fix the option to be the correct formalization</li>
	<li><strong>Useful draft for formalization:</strong> You would need to change quiet a few things, but it is better to start from this option, than from the original requirement</li>
	<li><strong>No help for formalization:</strong> The option does not help you and you would be better off formalizing the requirement completely by yourself</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
                <sid><![CDATA[892867]]></sid>
                <group_order><![CDATA[2]]></group_order>
                <randomization_group />
                <grelevance />
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[553]]></id>
                <gid><![CDATA[471]]></gid>
                <group_name><![CDATA[Metadata]]></group_name>
                <description />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
                <sid><![CDATA[892867]]></sid>
                <group_order><![CDATA[1]]></group_order>
                <randomization_group />
                <grelevance />
            </row>
        </rows>
    </group_l10ns>
