        </fields>
        <rows>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17899]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16730]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The list of requirements from [ND-E-67] that shall be explicitly verified by means of a verification control process (VCD / VCB) are listed in Appendix B.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17900]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16731]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The design of the Thermal Control shall be such that the Satellite can be developed, integrated and tested separately with minimum interactions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17901]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16732]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS design shall follow the requirements of [ND-E-67], unless otherwise specified.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17902]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16733]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>For Ground failure investigation it shall be possible to access and diagnose all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) without impacting the current mode.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17903]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16734]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Thermal Control shall ensure temperatures commensurate with survival of the Satellite and the FLORIS instrument during Emergency and Safe Mode conditions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17904]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16735]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>AOCS mode transitions during nominal operations shall be autonomous, except for the exit from initial acquisition in LEOP and the return from Emergency and Safe Mode.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17905]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16736]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Satellite on-board ephemeris table (e.g. Earth, Sun, stars) shall not require an update from Ground more frequently than once every 15 days.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17906]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16737]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Pointing performance, stability and robustness of the AOCS in all operational modes and mission phases shall be demonstrated in presence of the worst-case conditions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17907]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16738]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Thermal Control shall provide the thermal environment required to ensure the full performance for each mission phase and operational mode and for the complete duration of the mission.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17908]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16739]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The list of requirements from [ND-E-15] and [ND-E-65] that shall be explicitly verified by means of a verification control process (VCD/VCB) are listed in Appendix B.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17909]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16740]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Geodetic nadir pointing with yaw steering compensation shall be the nominal reference attitude profile.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17910]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16741]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The nominal operations of the AOCS shall be fully automatic and autonomous.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17911]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16742]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS FDIR shall autonomously inhibit anomalously long thruster firings.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17912]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16743]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The accuracy of the estimation and control of attitude, position, velocity and angular rates shall be derived from the observational, geo-location and co-registration requirements.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17913]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16744]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Thermal Control shall ensure the temperatures commensurate with decontamination of the FLORIS instrument, including LEOP.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17914]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16745]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS operation modes shall be defined in accordance with the Satellite functional and operational requirements and shall include an Emergency and Safe mode.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17915]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16746]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide all parameters required by the on-ground payload data processing in a self-contained dedicated Platform ancillary space packet (NAVATT) containing as a minimum the PVT solution in ECEF generated by the active GNSS unit at PPS and its validity.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17916]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16747]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Thermal Control shall fulfil the requirements of [ND-E-15], [ND-E-65] and the guidelines of [RD-12], unless otherwise specified.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17917]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16748]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If a navigation function is necessary for the mission, the AOCS shall provide the hardware and software means for autonomous on-board determination of the spacecraft orbital state which includes position, velocity and time.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17918]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16749]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS modes used for initial acquisition shall provide the capability for transition, from the initial attitude and rate after launcher separation to the final mission pointing.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17919]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16750]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide, as specified by the mission requirements, the hardware and software means for autonomous on-board attitude determination.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17920]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16751]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall ensure that the attitude guidance and pointing specified by the mission requirements, during the mission operational phase are met.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17921]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16752]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide during all phases of the mission the capability to acquire and keep all attitudes necessary to perform the mission.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17922]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16753]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall identify for every propulsion-based AOCS mode, the number of pulses commanded to the thruster, the associated pulse profiles and the total impulse.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17923]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16754]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the hardware and software capabilities and performances, to ensure the mission availability, as specified at satellite level.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17924]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16755]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall justify the hardware redundancy implemented against failure tolerance requirements and reliability requirements.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17925]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16756]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>For diagonal terms, the following convention should be used: ∫ I xx = ( y + z ) dm 2 2 , ∫ I yy = (z + x ) dm 2 2 , ∫ I zz = (x + y ) dm</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17926]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16757]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the hardware and software capabilities and performances, to ensure a safe state of the spacecraft.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17927]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16758]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the hardware and software capabilities and performances, to perform the orbit control manoeuvres, as specified by the mission requirements.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17928]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16759]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS software shall provide the capability to disable or enable, by ground command, any autonomous AOCS FDIR monitoring or action function.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17929]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16760]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall contribute to the estimation of remaining propellant quantities, through on-board or on-ground algorithms, when the measurement provided by the propulsion system does not cover the mission need.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17930]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16761]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS software shall provide the capability to modify by ground command the parameters of FDIR monitoring and actions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17931]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16762]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide to satellite FDIR, for the purpose of failure monitoring, parameters observed on AOCS units or derived from AOCS embedded algorithms.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17932]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16763]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall contribute to the satellite FDIR definition through identification of AOCS failure cases, monitoring means and policy, recovery means and policy.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17933]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16764]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>For inertia cross-products, one of the following usual conventions should be used : ∫ I xy = − xy dm , ∫ I xz = − xz dm , ∫ I yz = − yz dm or: ∫ Pxy = + xy dm , ∫ Pxz = + xz dm , ∫ Pyz = + yz dm</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17934]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16765]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall implement actions on AOCS units and AOCS modes required by the satellite FDIR in case of anomaly.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17935]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16766]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>At satellite level, it shall be demonstrated that the AOCS design is compatible with other functional chains for the attitudes and durations.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17936]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16767]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall define an unambiguous sign convention for inertia to be used throughout the AOCS documentation.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17937]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16768]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It shall be demonstrated that the AOCS design does not prevent meeting the requirements imposed by the mission and payload constraints.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17938]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16769]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall define a strategy for the implementation of the mode transitions and describe how this strategy is applied for each AOCS mode transition.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17939]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16770]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Transitions between modes shall be triggered by one of the following mechanisms: 
1. TC: by ground request (Time tagged or not), 
2. AUTO: autonomously on board, after checking a transition condition, 
3. FDIR: after failure detection.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17940]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16771]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The capability shall be provided to inhibit or to force Auto and FDIR transitions by TC.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17941]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16772]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall process and deliver the attitude and orbit related information to other on-board functions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17942]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16773]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS design shall meet calibration constraints from mission or payload needs.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17943]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16774]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the capability to perform end-of-life disposal.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17944]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16775]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>A mapping of AOCS modes into satellite modes shall be described, to clarify all the possible configurations in which the satellite can be in relation with the AOCS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17945]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16776]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The entry into safe mode shall be commandable by ground TC.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17946]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16777]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The return from safe mode shall be commandable by ground TC.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17947]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16778]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>In case of major anomaly, the AOCS shall provide the autonomous capability to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft vital functions, including power, thermal and communications.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17948]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16779]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the capability for achieving orbit control manoeuvres specified by mission analysis.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17949]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16780]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The AOCS shall provide the hardware and software capabilities and performances, to perform the attitude measurement, estimation, guidance and control needed for the mission.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17950]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16781]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed and constructed so that the rate for Loss of Thrust (or Power) Control (LOTC/LOPC) events, consistent with the safety objective associated with the intended aircraft application, can be achieved.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17951]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16782]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The magnitude of any change in thrust or power and the associated transition time must be identified and described in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17952]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16783]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be demonstrated that, when a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the change occurs so that, if the flight crew is required to initiate, respond to or be aware of the Control Mode change, there must be provision for a means to alert the crew.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17953]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16784]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be demonstrated that, when a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the change occurs so that the Engine does not surge, stall, flame-out or experience unacceptable thrust or power changes or oscillations, or other unacceptable characteristics.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17954]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16785]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be demonstrated that, when a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the change occurs so that the Engine does not exceed any of its operating limitations.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17955]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16786]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Means for shutting down the Engine rapidly must be provided.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17956]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16787]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>All associated software and encoded logic must be designed, implemented and verified to minimise the existence of errors by using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17957]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16788]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>When complying with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, a system safety assessment must be completed for the Engine Control System. This assessment must identify Faults or Failures that result in a change in thrust or power, a transmission of erroneous data, or an effect on Engine operability together with the predicted frequency of occurrence of these Faults or Failures.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17958]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16789]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed so that the loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System will not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17959]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16790]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which allows modulation of Engine power or thrust with adequate sensitivity and accuracy over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17960]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16791]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>When electronic over-speed protection systems are provided, the design must include a means for testing the system to establish the A13:A15 availability of the protection function. The means must be such that a complete test of the system can be achieved in the minimum number of cycles. If the test is not fully automatic, the specification for a manual test must be contained in the Engine instructions for operation.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17961]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16792]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed so that the loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System will not cause the unacceptable transmission of erroneous data.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17962]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16793]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed and constructed so that in the Full-up Configuration, the system is essentially single Fault tolerant for electrical and electronic Failures with respect to LOTC/LOPC events.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17963]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16794]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Single Failures leading to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, must not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect for any Engine.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17964]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16795]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The need for, and the characteristics of, any electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for starting and operating the Engine, including transient and steady state voltage limits, must be identified and declared in the Engine instructions for installation.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17965]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16796]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>When over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, it must be demonstrated by test or other acceptable means that the over-speed function remains available between inspection and maintenance periods.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17966]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16797]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>When an Engine dedicated power source is required for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1), its capacity should provide sufficient margin to account for Engine operation below idle where the Engine Control System is designed and expected to recover Engine operation automatically. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17967]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16798]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Engines having a 30-Second OEI Power Rating must incorporate means or provision for means for automatic availability and automatic control of the 30-Second OEI Power within its operating limitations.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17968]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16799]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Low voltage transients outside of the power supply voltage limitations, declared under CS-E 50 (h)(3), must meet the specifications of CS-E 50 (h)(1). The Engine Control System must resume normal operation when aircraft supplied electrical power returns to within the declared limits.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17969]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16800]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which does not create unacceptable thrust or power oscillations.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17970]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16801]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The effects of blockage or leakage of the signal lines on the Engine Control System must be considered as part of the system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) and the appropriate design precautions adopted.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17971]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16802]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed and constructed so that foreseeable Failures or malfunctions leading to local events in the intended aircraft installation, such as fire, overheat, or Failures leading to damage to Engine Control System components, must not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect due to Engine Control System Failures or malfunctions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17972]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16803]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Single Failures leading to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, must be detected and accommodated. The accommodation strategy must not result in an unacceptable change in thrust or power or an unacceptable change in Engine operating and starting characteristics. The effects of these Failures on Engine power or thrust, Engine operability and starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope must be evaluated and documented. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17973]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16804]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Engine Control System must be designed and constructed so that Single Failures of Engine Control System components do not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17974]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16805]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which enables selected values of relevant control parameters to be maintained.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17975]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16806]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should be able to determine the public holidays in Germany from January 01 2017 until December 31 2027 (at least). Then, the federal state must be configurable since there are different regulations for public holidays in the various parts of the country.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17976]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16807]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate starting from January 01 2017 until December 31 2027 (at least).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17977]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16808]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet by the following formula:
hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek. The period can be a week or a month, depending on the TimesheetFreqeuency of the contract. E.g., if workingDaysPerWeek = 5, Monday to Friday count as working days, Saturday and Sunday as non-working days. Only public holidays have to be counted that are on working days.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17978]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16809]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project participants should record the time spent on the project.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17979]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16810]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Decisions made to detail and/or change requirements shall be documented in the project manual.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17980]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16811]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project manual should contain descriptions of problems that occurred during the implementation and their solutions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17981]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16812]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project manual shall contain a list of completed/missed requirements.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17982]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16813]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall calculate the total hours due for the contract as the sum of the hours due of the individual Timesheets.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17983]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16814]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall be documented in a project manual (can be online, e.g., Wiki) such that the customer can install the system on a fresh Payara server.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17984]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16815]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project team shall prefix all global names with its team name. Such names are e.g. project name, context path (root URL), database name, persistence units, server resources, etc. This is to avoid naming conflicts, since the customer has to install the systems of many teams side-by-side.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17985]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16816]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project team shall document architectural decisions, e.g., which subsystems do exist, how is the source code structured, etc., in the project manual.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17986]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16817]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall use one of the database servers MySQL (preferred), PostgreSql, or JavaDB/Derby.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17987]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16818]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall use third-party libraries that were not presented in the lecture/lab only after negotiation with the customer.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17988]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16819]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should collect all reminders so that a person receives at most one e-mail per day.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17989]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16820]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>On the last day of a time sheet (either end of week or end of month), the TSS shall send a reminder mail to the employee if the time sheet is in state IN_PROGRESS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17990]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16821]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide assistants and supervisors with the ability to request changes to a time sheet that is in status SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE. Then, the time sheet changes to IN_PROGRESS status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17991]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16822]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should provide employees with the ability to revoke the signature. Then, the time sheet changes from SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE to IN_PROGRESS status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17992]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16823]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide employees with the ability to sign a time sheet. Then, the time sheet changes from IN_PROGRESS to SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17993]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16824]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide employees, assistants, supervisors, and secretaries with the ability to view time sheets.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17994]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16825]]></qid>
