                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17998]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16829]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should support German as user interface language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[17999]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16830]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall be designed in a way that only authorized users may view/change/delete data. Access rules are based on the users affiliation (staff, student) as well as on the roles a user owns with respect to a contract.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18000]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16831]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide employees, assistants, supervisors, and secretaries with the ability to view contract statistics (e.g., sum of hours due, balance).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18001]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16832]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide supervisors with the ability to sign a time sheet that is in status SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE. Then, the time sheet changes to SIGNED_BY_SUPERVISOR status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18002]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16833]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall calculate the vacation hours by the following formula:
vacationHours = vacationDaysPerYear * durationOfContract / 12 * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek. The duration of the contract is counted in months.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18003]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16834]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall delete time sheets 2 years after the signature of the supervisor. When all time sheets of a contract are deleted, the contract has to be deleted as well.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18004]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16835]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should send reminders to users in their preferred language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18005]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16836]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall support English as user interface language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18006]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16837]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall authenticate users prior to giving access to any data.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18007]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16838]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should support mobile devices.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18008]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16839]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should provide employees and supervisors with the ability to digitally sign the time sheets.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18009]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16840]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should be designed such that it can be used with different browsers. At least, FireFox, Safari, Chrome shall be supported.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18010]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16841]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall be designed such that the user interface language can be switched.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18011]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16842]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should support variable archive durations. In this case, the 2 years duration is not fixed, but must be stored per contract. The duration should have a default value of 2 years.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18012]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16843]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Before terminating a contract, the TSS should warn the user if there are time sheets in state IN_PROGRESS that have entries. The user may then decide to not terminate the contract yet.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18013]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16844]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall ensure that start date and end date of a contract always denote complete months (i.e., the start date must be the first day of a month, the end date the last day).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18014]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16845]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should use the Bootstrap CSS library.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18015]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16846]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should provide the users to choose their language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18016]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16847]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall support at least two user interface languages.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18017]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16848]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide employees with the ability to manage their time sheet entries. Changes to entries are only allowed when a Timesheet is IN_PROGRESS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18018]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16849]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should provide secretaries with the ability to print contracts. This printout is intended to be used as cover page for the paper archive of the printed time sheets.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18019]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16850]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide secretaries with the ability to archive time sheets that are in status SIGNED_BY_SUPERVISOR. Then, the time sheet changes to status ARCHIVED.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18020]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16851]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall delete time sheets in status IN_PROGRESS as soon as the contract status changes to TERMINATED.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18021]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16852]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall not delete time sheets that are in the SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE state.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18022]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16853]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall record the date of termination of a contract.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18023]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16854]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall create all time sheets for a contract based on the time sheet frequency and the start and end dates of the contract as soon as the contract enters the STARTED status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18024]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16855]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall not delete time sheets that are in the SIGNED_BY_SUPERVISOR state.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18025]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16856]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall calculate the total hours due, the vacation hours, the remaining hours due and take into account weekends and public holidays.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18026]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16857]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall send a reminder mail to the supervisor and the assistants if the time
sheet is in state SIGNED_BY_EMPLOYEE. (then, the supervisor may reject or sign the
time sheet)</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18027]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16858]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall be able to determine whether a person is university staff member.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18028]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16859]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall send a reminder mail to the secretaries if the time sheet is in state
SIGNED_BY_SUPERVISOR.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18029]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16860]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS should repeat reminders every day.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18030]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16861]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide assistants and supervisors with the ability to start a contract. Then, the contract changes from PREPARED to STARTED status. All Timesheets are created in status IN_PROGRESS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18031]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16862]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall ensure that time sheet entries can only be added, changed, and removed when the time sheet is in IN_PROGRESS status and the contract of the time sheet is in STARTED status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18032]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16863]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall set a contract to status ARCHIVED as soon as all time sheets of that contract are in status ARCHIVED.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18033]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16864]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall set a contract to PREPARED status as soon as it is created.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18034]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16865]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall ensure that only contracts can be terminated whose time sheets are in status SIGNED_BY_SUPERVISOR or IN_PROGRESS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18035]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16866]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide assistants and supervisors with the ability to terminate a started contract. Then, the contract changes from STARTED to ABORTED status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18036]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16867]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall ensure that start date, end date, frequency, hours per week, vacation hours, working days per week, and vacation days per year can only be changed when the contract is in PREPARED status.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18037]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16868]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The TSS shall provide assistants and supervisors with the ability to manage contracts. Manage means „CRUD“ (Create, Read, Update, Delete). Update and deletion of contracts is only possible in state PREPARED.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18038]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16869]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The state of a poll shall be one of PREPARED, STARTED, VOTING, FINISHED. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18039]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16870]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The individual team members should record the time spent on the project.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18040]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16871]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Decisions made to change requirements shall be documented in the project manual. E.g., if you feel that the requirements are not detailed enough, you may add more details.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18041]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16872]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project manual should contain descriptions of any problems that occurred during the implementation.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18042]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16873]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project manual shall contain a list of completed/missed requirements. For the missed requirements, there has to be a rationale.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18043]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16874]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be documented in a project manual (can be online, e.g., gitlab Wiki) so that the supervisor can install the system on fresh Payara and MariaDB servers.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18044]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16875]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that access to polls is only granted to the related organizers and administrators. Administrators may see only the poll title, voting period, and the organizers.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18045]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16876]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should be designed in a way that network communication with the database server is encrypted.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18046]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16877]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The items of a question shall have a short name and an optional description.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18047]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16878]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that network communication with its users (administrators, organizers, participants) is encrypted (HTTPS protocol).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18048]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16879]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If LDAP is not used, the EVS shall be designed in a way that all passwords are stored in hashed/encrypted form.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18049]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16880]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Java naming conventions shall be followed strictly</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18050]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16881]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The project team shall prefix all global names with its team name. Such names are e.g., project name, context path (root URL), database name, persistence units, server resources, etc. This is to avoid naming conflicts, since the supervisor has to install the systems of many teams sideby-side.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18051]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16882]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The naming conventions for projects, JavaEE modules, database connection pools, databases, and other files and resources shall be followed strictly.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18052]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16883]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall use one of the database servers MariaDB/MySQL (preferred), PostgreSQL, or JavaDB/Derby.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18053]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16884]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The team shall ask for consent prior to using third-party libraries that were not presented in the lecture/ lab. Usage is permitted only after negotiation with the supervisor. Libraries that may be used without prior consent are: PrimeFaces, RichFaces, BootsFaces, Redirect, Bootstrap CSS, JQuery.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18054]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16885]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall contain (at least) two modules, i.e., a web module and an EJB module.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18055]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16886]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be implemented according to the layered architecture and the architectural rules provided in the document evs-architecture.pdf.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18056]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16887]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should send notification and reminder mails to participants in their preferred language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18057]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16888]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The questions of a poll shall have a title (titles have to be unique with scope poll).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18058]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16889]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should support multilingual text also in the data items (e.g., title, short name, description of polls, questions, and items) so that the participants can view their options in their preferred language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18059]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16890]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall support German as user interface language. The project team may decide to use a different second language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18060]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16891]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall support English as user interface language.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18061]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16892]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall support at least two user interface languages.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18062]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16893]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If the language switch done on user request, the EVS should remember the user’s language setting.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18063]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16894]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The language switch shall be realized either by an URL prefix, by detecting the client browser’s language setting, or on user request (preferred language setting).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18064]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16895]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that the user interface language can be switched.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18065]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16896]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should be designed in a way that it supports mobile device browsers (limited display area, portrait page display instead of landscape).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18066]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16897]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that it supports at least one of the following desktop/laptop web browsers: FireFox, Safari, Chrome in the most recent stable version available at delivery of the project.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18067]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16898]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should use advanced technologies (e.g., AJAX) supported by JSF components to enhance user experience.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18068]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16899]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should use third-party JSF components (e.g., bootsFaces, myFaces, richFaces).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18069]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16900]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should use third-party CSS libraries (such as Bootstrap).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18070]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16901]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to define the minimum and maximum number of choices for MULTIPLE CHOICE questions.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18071]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16902]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be implemented using the JSF technology. This means it’s not permitted to use JavaScript frameworks like Angular or React.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18072]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16903]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should display the results in graphical form (e.g., as pie chart).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18073]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16904]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall show the number of votes for each item of each question of a poll, the number of abstentions, and the voter participation in the result view.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18074]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16905]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The length of the random part of the result hyperlink shall be equal to or greater than 16 characters. This is to make it very very improbable that anybody can forge or guess a valid result link.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18075]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16906]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The result notification email shall contain a randomized result hyperlink to the results page.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18076]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16907]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as the results of a poll are published, the EVS shall send a notification email to all participants and organizers of the poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18077]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16908]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as a poll is FINISHED and the number of submitted votes is at least 3, the EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to publish the results.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18078]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16909]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As long as a poll is not FINISHED, the EVS shall ensure that nobody is able to view (intermediate) results.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18079]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16910]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that nobody is able to view results of polls with less than 3 submitted votes.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18080]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16911]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as a poll is FINISHED and the number of submitted votes is at least 3, the EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to view the results of a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18081]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16912]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The system shall provide organizers to add different types of questions to a poll.
• SINGLE CHOICE with two or more items and one choice
• MULTIPLE CHOICE with two or more items
• YES/NO question with two items “yes” and “no” and one choice (indeed, this is a special case of SINGLE CHOICE questions)</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18082]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16913]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The system should provide participants with the ability to abstain from voting for a complete poll (this is equivalent to abstention from all questions).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18083]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16914]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide participants with the ability to abstain from voting (Enthaltung oder ungültige Stimme) for each question of a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18084]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16915]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that subsequent participants using the same browser window can not restore the previous choices (e.g., by the „go back“ function or auto fill capabilities of browsers).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18085]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16916]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall discard all choices of a cancelled voting.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18086]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16917]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide participants with the ability to cancel a voting, e.g., by closing the browser, or by clicking a cancel button. The token used in cancelled voting shall be re-useable later.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18087]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16918]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that participants can not change their vote after submitting.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18088]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16919]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as the vote was submitted, the EVS shall invalidate the token used for that vote, i.e., the token can’t be re-used.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18089]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16920]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall present a button to submit a vote.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18090]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16921]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If a poll to clone has results, the EVS shall not clone the results.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18091]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16922]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as the token was verified, the EVS shall display the questions and items.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18092]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16923]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If a poll to clone has votes, the EVS shall not clone the votes.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18093]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16924]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If the voting page is accessed by the link in the notification email, the token input field should be pre-filled (see requirement PL04.2).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18094]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16925]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The voting page shall present an input field for a participant’s token.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18095]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16926]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should provide organizers with the ability to clone a poll (period, description, questions, participant list).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18096]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16927]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As long as a poll is in state VOTING, the EVS shall provide a web page to submit a vote.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18097]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16928]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If participation tracking is enabled for a poll, the EVS should provide organizers with the ability to activate automatic reminders to participants who didn’t vote.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18098]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16929]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that a token that was previously issued can never be re-generated.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18099]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16930]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that all tokens are unique in the scope of the whole system.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18100]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16931]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to track the participations for a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18101]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16932]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure anonymity. At any point in time, it shall be impossible to identify which participant submitted which vote. This also shall to be guaranteed for polls with participation tracking.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18102]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16933]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The system shall ensure that a token can not be associated with a vote.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18103]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16934]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The length of the tokens shall be equal to or greater than 16 characters. This is to make it very improbable that a valid token can be forged or guessed.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18104]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16935]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If the poll is not in state PREPARED, the EVS shall ensure that the participants of the poll can not be changed.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18105]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16936]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to group arbitrary many questions into a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18106]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16937]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be designed in a way that the stored participant lists are private to each organizer.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18107]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16938]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as a poll is started, the EVS shall assign a random token to each participant of a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18108]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16939]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to store participant lists for easy reuse in subsequent polls.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18109]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16940]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each stored participant list shall have a unique name (scope is per organizer).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18110]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16941]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should provide organizers with the ability to comfortably create participant lists, e.g., by pasting email addresses from other applications such as spread sheets or KLIPS.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18111]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16942]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The notification email should contain a hyperlink that already contains a pre-filled token of the participant so that the participant can immediately begin to vote.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18112]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16943]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as a poll is started by an organizer, the EVS shall send a notification email to each participant. (The university’s mail server shall not be „mis-used“, it’s recommended to use the dummy/test SMTP server provided with the task)</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18113]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16944]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The notification email shall contain the poll title, description, voting period, the participant’s voting token, and a hyperlink to the voting page.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18114]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16945]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As long as a poll is in state PREPARED, the EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to delete participants from the participants of a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18115]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16946]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should provide organizers with the ability to add participants from outside the university.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18116]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16947]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that organizers authenticate themselves with username and password. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18117]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16948]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that organizers only can work on polls that they own. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18118]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16949]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each poll shall be owned by at least one organizer (the creator is the initial owner). </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18119]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16950]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to create arbitrary many polls.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18120]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16951]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should provide organizers with the ability to preview their polls in the participant view.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18121]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16952]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall be able to identify university employees using the LDAP service provided by the GHRKO computing center. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18122]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16953]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that an organizer can not remove herself from the organizer list. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18123]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16954]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each participant shall be identified by a valid email address.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18124]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16955]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As long as a poll is in state PREPARED, the EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to add arbitrary many participants to a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18125]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16956]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS should provide organizers with the ability to add further organizers to a poll. The poll is then owned by each of the organizers</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18126]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16957]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If LDAP is not used, the EVS shall provide administrators with the ability to manage organizer accounts (see OR01.2).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18127]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16958]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If a poll to-delete is not in state PREPARED or FINISHED, the EVS shall send a notification email to all organizers and participants to inform about the removal.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18128]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16959]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide all university employees with the ability to act as organizers. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18129]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16960]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each poll shall have a title. The title has to be unique (scope is system).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18130]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16961]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that administrators can not access votes and results of polls that they don’t own.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18131]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16962]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide administrators with the ability to delete any poll (including all votes and results).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18132]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16963]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as a poll has at least 3 participants and is in state PREPARED, the EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to start the poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18133]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16964]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as the voting period starts, the EVS shall set the poll state to VOTING. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18134]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16965]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>If a poll to-delete is not in state PREPARED or FINISHED, the EVS shall send a notification email to all organizers and participants to inform them about the removal.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18135]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16966]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as an organizer account is deleted, the EVS shall delete all polls that belong exclusively to that organizer (Polls with multiple organizers are not deleted.)</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18136]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16967]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that the participant list of a poll can only be changed in state PREPARED. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18137]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16968]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each poll shall have a voting period (start and end date with time).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18138]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16969]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to extend (but not shorten) the voting period when a poll is in state STARTED or VOTING. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18139]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16970]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as an organizer starts a poll, the EVS shall set the poll state to STARTED. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18140]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16971]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>Each poll shall have a description.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18141]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16972]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that the description, initial voting period, questions, and participant list of a poll can only be changed in state PREPARED. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18142]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16973]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall ensure that there are no duplicate entries in the participants of a poll.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18143]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16974]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to delete a poll (including all votes and results).</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18144]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16975]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The number of questions of a poll shall be at least 1.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18145]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16976]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The EVS shall provide organizers with the ability to change the organizer list. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18146]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16977]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>As soon as the voting period ends or all participants have submitted their vote, the EVS shall set the poll state to FINISHED. </strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18147]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16978]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Electronic Voting System (EVS) shall provide organizers to conduct electronic polls.</strong></p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18148]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16979]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The list of requirements from [ND-E-67] that shall be explicitly verified by means of a verification control process (VCD / VCB) are listed in Appendix B.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18149]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16980]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The list of requirements from [ND-E-67] that shall be explicitly verified by means of a verification control process (VCD / VCB) are listed in Appendix B.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18150]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16981]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The explicit verification method for the requirements from [ND-E-67] shall be the verification control process (VCD/VCB).</p><p>The location of the list of requirements from [ND-E-67] that shall be explicitly verified by means of the verification control process (VCD/VCB) shall be Appendix B.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18151]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16982]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>Appendix B shall list the requirements from [ND-E-67] that shall be verified by VCD/VCB.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18152]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16983]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a requirement from [ND-E-67] is listed in Appendix B, the verification team shall explicitly verify the requirement by means of a verification control process (VCD/VCB).</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18153]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16984]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The design of the Thermal Control shall be such that the Satellite can be developed, integrated and tested separately with minimum interactions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18154]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16985]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall be designed in a way the Satellite can be developed, integrated and tested separately with minimum interactions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18155]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16986]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The number of interactions of the Thermal Control Subsystem with other subsystems shall be less than or equal to value.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18156]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16987]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall enable separate development of the Satellite with minimal interactions.</p><p>The Thermal Control shall enable separate integration of the Satellite with minimal interactions.</p><p>The Thermal Control shall enable separate testing of the Satellite with minimal interactions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18157]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16988]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall be designed in a way that the Satellite development can be operated with interactions being minimum.</p><p>The Thermal Control shall be designed in a way that the Satellite integration can be operated with interactions being minimum.</p><p>The Thermal Control shall be designed in a way that the Satellite testing can be operated with interactions being minimum.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18158]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16989]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS design shall follow the requirements of [ND-E-67], unless otherwise specified.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18159]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16990]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall comply with [ND-E-67].</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18160]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16991]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If no other specification is provided, the system AOCS shall comply with [ND-E-67] for the AOCS design only.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18161]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16992]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If not otherwise specified, the AOCS design shall follow the requirements of [ND-E-67].</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18162]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16993]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall follow the requirements of [ND-E-67].</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18163]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16994]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>For ground failure investigation, the system shall be able to access and diagnose all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) without impacting the current mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18164]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16995]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the system is in Ground failure investigation mode, the AOCS shall be able to provide the ability to access and diagnose all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) without impacting the current mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18165]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16996]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the system is in the state Ground Failure Investigation, the system shall access all nominal and redundant AOCS units.</p><p>As long as the system is in the state Ground Failure Investigation, the system shall diagnose all nominal and redundant AOCS units.</p><p>As long as the system is in the state Ground Failure Investigation, the system shall maintain the current mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18166]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16997]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as ground failure investigation is in progress, the system shall provide the ground investigation team with the ability to access all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) without impacting the current mode.</p><p>As long as ground failure investigation is in progress, the system shall provide the ground investigation team with the ability to diagnose all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) without impacting the current mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18167]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16998]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide ground with the ability to access all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) for ground failure investigation without impacting the current mode.</p><p>The AOCS shall provide ground with the ability to diagnose all AOCS units (nominal and redundant) for ground failure investigation without impacting the current mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18168]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[16999]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall ensure the temperature is commensurate with the survival of the Satellite.</p><p>The Thermal Control shall ensure the temperature is commensurate with the survival of the FLORIS instrument.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18169]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17000]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the system is in Emergency mode, the Thermal Control shall ensure temperatures are commensurate with the survival of the Satellite and the FLORIS instrument.</p><p>As long as the system is in Safe Mode, the Thermal Control shall ensure temperatures are commensurate with the survival of the Satellite and the FLORIS instrument.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18170]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17001]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the Satellite is in the state Emergency Mode or as long as the Satellite is in the state Safe Mode, the system Thermal Control subsystem shall maintain the temperature of the Satellite commensurate with survival.</p><p>As long as the Satellite is in the state Emergency Mode or as long as the Satellite is in the state Safe Mode, the system Thermal Control subsystem shall maintain the temperature of the FLORIS instrument commensurate with survival.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18171]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17002]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>During Emergency and Safe Mode conditions, the Thermal Control shall maintain the temperature of the Satellite within the survival range.</p><p>During Emergency and Safe Mode conditions, the Thermal Control shall maintain the temperature of the FLORIS instrument within the survival range.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18172]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17003]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as in Emergency or Safe Mode conditions, the Thermal Control shall ensure temperatures commensurate with survival of the Satellite.</p><p>As long as in Emergency or Safe Mode conditions, the Thermal Control shall ensure temperatures commensurate with survival of the FLORIS instrument.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18173]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17004]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>AOCS mode transitions during nominal operations shall be autonomous, except for the exit from initial acquisition in LEOP and the return from Emergency and Safe Mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18174]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17005]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the system is operating in nominal mode, the AOCS shall perform mode transitions autonomously.</p><p>As soon as the AOCS exits initial acquisition during LEOP, the system shall be able to transition modes non-autonomously.</p><p>As soon as the system returns from Emergency and Safe Mode, the AOCS shall be able to transition modes autonomously.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18175]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17006]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the AOCS is in the state Nominal Operations, the AOCS shall perform mode transitions autonomously.</p><p>If the AOCS exits the state Initial Acquisition in LEOP or if the AOCS exits the state Emergency Mode or if the AOCS exits the state Safe Mode, the system AOCS shall inhibit autonomous mode transitions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18176]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17007]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as AOCS is in nominal operations and as long as AOCS is not exiting initial acquisition in LEOP and as long as AOCS is not returning from Emergency and Safe Mode, the AOCS mode transitions shall be autonomous.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18177]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17008]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as in nominal operations, the AOCS shall perform mode transitions autonomously.</p><p>The AOCS shall perform mode transition to exit from initial acquisition in LEOP not autonomously.</p><p>The AOCS shall perform mode transition to return from Emergency mode not autonomously.</p><p>The AOCS shall perform mode transition to return from Safe mode not autonomously.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18178]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17009]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The satellite on-board ephemeris table shall be updated no more frequently than once every 15 days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18179]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17010]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The satellite on-board ephemeris table shall be updated from the Ground no more frequently than once every 15 days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18180]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17011]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The maximum update interval from Ground of the satellite on-board ephemeris table (e.g., Earth, Sun, stars) shall be less than or equal to 15 days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18181]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17012]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The ground system shall update the satellite on-board ephemeris table (e.g. Earth, Sun, stars) no more frequently than once every 15 days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18182]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17013]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The update interval of the satellite on-board ephemeris table shall be &gt;= 15 days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18183]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17014]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The pointing performance, stability, and robustness of the AOCS shall be demonstrated in all operational modes and mission phases under worst-case conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18184]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17015]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall demonstrate pointing performance, stability, and robustness in all operational modes and mission phases under worst-case conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18185]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17016]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Pointing performance, stability and robustness of the AOCS in all operational modes and mission phases shall be demonstrated in presence of the worst-case conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18186]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17017]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If worst-case conditions are present, the AOCS shall demonstrate pointing performance in all operational modes and mission phases.</p><p>If worst-case conditions are present, the AOCS shall demonstrate stability in all operational modes and mission phases.</p><p>If worst-case conditions are present, the AOCS shall demonstrate robustness in all operational modes and mission phases.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18187]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17018]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The test team shall test the pointing performance of the AOCS in all operational modes in all mission phases under worst-case conditions.</p><p>The test team shall test the stability of the AOCS in all operational modes in all mission phases under worst-case conditions.</p><p>The test team shall test the robustness of the AOCS in all operational modes in all mission phases under worst-case conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18188]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17019]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall provide the thermal environment required to ensure full performance during each mission phase and operational mode for the complete duration of the mission.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18189]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17020]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall provide the thermal environment required to ensure full performance for each mission phase and operational mode as long as the system is in the respective mission phase and operational mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18190]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17021]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system Thermal Control shall provide the thermal environment required to ensure full performance for each mission phase and operational mode and for the complete duration of the mission.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18191]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17022]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall maintain the thermal environment such that the system meets all performance requirements for each mission phase and operational mode during the complete mission duration.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18192]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17023]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Thermal Control shall provide the thermal environment for full performance.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18193]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17024]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The list of requirements from [ND-E-15] and [ND-E-65] that shall be explicitly verified by means of a verification control process (VCD/VCB) are listed in Appendix B.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
