            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18384]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17215]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall be able to return from safe mode by command via ground TC.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18385]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17216]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall provide ground TC with the ability to command the return from the state Safe Mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18386]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17217]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall be able to receive commands from ground TC to return from safe mode.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18387]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17218]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide ground with the ability to command return from safe mode by ground TC.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18388]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17219]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a major anomaly occurs, the AOCS shall be able to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft vital functions.</p><p>The AOCS shall provide autonomous capability for power system during major anomaly.</p><p>The AOCS shall provide autonomous capability for thermal system during major anomaly.</p><p>The AOCS shall provide autonomous capability for communications system during major anomaly.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18389]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17220]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a major anomaly occurs, the AOCS shall be able to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft's power system.</p><p>If a major anomaly occurs, the AOCS shall be able to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft's thermal system.</p><p>If a major anomaly occurs, the AOCS shall be able to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft's communications system.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18390]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17221]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as the event major anomaly happens, the system AOCS shall be able to ensure the integrity of the spacecraft vital functions, including power, thermal and communications, autonomously.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18391]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17222]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a major anomaly occurs, the AOCS shall autonomously ensure the integrity of the spacecraft vital functions, including power, thermal, and communications.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18392]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17223]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a major anomaly happens, the AOCS shall ensure the integrity of the spacecraft vital functions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18393]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17224]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide the ability to perform orbit control manoeuvres as specified by mission analysis.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18394]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17225]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide the capability for achieving orbit control manoeuvres specified by mission analysis.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18395]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17226]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system AOCS shall execute orbit control manoeuvres specified by mission analysis.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18396]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17227]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall perform orbit control manoeuvres specified by mission analysis.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18397]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17228]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall be able to achieve orbit control manoeuvres specified by mission analysis.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18398]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17229]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide the ability to perform attitude measurement, estimation, guidance and control.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18399]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17230]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall provide the hardware and software capabilities to perform attitude measurement, estimation, guidance and control.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18400]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17231]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system AOCS subsystem shall measure the spacecraft attitude.</p><p>The system AOCS subsystem shall estimate the spacecraft attitude.</p><p>The system AOCS subsystem shall generate attitude guidance.</p><p>The system AOCS subsystem shall control the spacecraft attitude.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18401]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17232]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall measure attitude for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall estimate attitude for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall generate attitude guidance for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall control attitude for the mission.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18402]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17233]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The AOCS shall be able to perform the attitude measurement needed for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall be able to perform the estimation needed for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall be able to perform the guidance needed for the mission.</p><p>The AOCS shall be able to perform the control needed for the mission.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18403]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17234]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed and constructed so that the rate for Loss of Thrust Control (LOTC) or Loss of Power Control (LOPC) events can achieve the safety objective consistent with the intended aircraft application.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18404]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17235]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall achieve a rate of Loss of Thrust (or Power) Control (LOTC/LOPC) events consistent with the safety objective associated with the intended aircraft application.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18405]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17236]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The rate of Loss of Thrust or Power Control (LOTC/LOPC) events of the Engine Control System shall be consistent with the safety objective associated with the intended aircraft application.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18406]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17237]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System's LOTC/LOPC event rate shall be consistent with the safety objective for the intended aircraft application.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18407]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17238]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall achieve the rate for Loss of Thrust (or Power) Control (LOTC/LOPC) events consistent with the safety objective associated with the intended aircraft application.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18408]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17239]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The magnitude of any change in thrust or power and the associated transition time shall be identified and described in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18409]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17240]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The magnitude of any change in thrust or power shall be identified and described in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p><p>The transition time associated with any change in thrust or power shall be identified and described in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18410]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17241]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The magnitude of any change in thrust or power and the associated transition time must be identified and described in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18411]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17242]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall document the magnitude of any change in thrust or power and the associated transition time in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18412]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17243]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The DOA shall describe the magnitude of any change in thrust or power in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p><p>The DOA shall describe the associated transition time of any change in thrust or power in the Engine instructions for installation and operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18413]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17244]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a fault or failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall provide the flight crew with the ability to detect the mode change.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18414]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17245]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a fault or failure causes a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall provide the flight crew with the ability to receive an alert.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18415]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17246]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a change occurs from one Control Mode to another or as soon as a change occurs from one channel to another or as soon as a change occurs from the Primary System to the Back-up System and if a Fault is present or if a Failure is present and if the flight crew is required to initiate the Control Mode change or if the flight crew is required to respond to the Control Mode change or if the flight crew is required to be aware of the Control Mode change, the system shall alert the flight crew.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18416]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17247]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a fault or failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another or from one channel to another or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, and if the flight crew is required to initiate, respond to or be aware of the Control Mode change, the verification shall demonstrate that the system provides a means to alert the crew.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18417]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17248]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System and the flight crew is required to initiate, respond to or be aware of the Control Mode change, the Engine Control System shall be able to alert the crew.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18418]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17249]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not surge.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not stall.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not flame-out.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a switch between control modes, channels, or systems, the system shall prevent unacceptable thrust or power changes in the Engine.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition between Control Modes, channels, or primary and backup systems, the system shall avoid unacceptable oscillations in the Engine.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure leads to a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall avoid other unacceptable characteristics in the Engine.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18419]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17250]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not surge.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not stall.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not flame-out.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not experience unacceptable thrust changes.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not experience unacceptable power changes.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not experience unacceptable oscillations.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a transition from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not exhibit other unacceptable characteristics.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18420]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17251]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>It must be demonstrated that, when a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the change occurs so that the Engine does not surge, stall, flame-out or experience unacceptable thrust or power changes or oscillations, or other unacceptable characteristics.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18421]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17252]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a fault or failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall prevent the engine from surging, stalling, flaming out, or experiencing unacceptable thrust or power changes, oscillations, or other unacceptable characteristics.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18422]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17253]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine Control System shall prevent the engine from stall.</p><p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine Control System shall prevent the engine from flame-out.</p><p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine Control System shall prevent the engine from unacceptable thrust or power changes or oscillations.</p><p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine Control System shall prevent the engine from unacceptable characteristics.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18423]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17254]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as the system changes from one Control Mode to another, switches channels, or transitions from the Primary System to the Back-up System due to a Fault or Failure, the system shall prevent the Engine from exceeding its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18424]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17255]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a switch from one Control Mode to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not exceed any of its operating limitations.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a switch from one channel to another, the system shall ensure the Engine does not exceed any of its operating limitations.</p><p>As soon as a fault or failure causes a switch from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the system shall ensure the Engine does not exceed any of its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18425]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17256]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as the event change of control mode due to a fault or failure happens or as soon as the event change of channel due to a fault or failure happens or as soon as the event change from the primary system to the backup system due to a fault or failure happens, the system shall prevent the engine from exceeding any operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18426]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17257]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a fault or failure causes a change from one Control Mode to another or if a fault or failure causes a change from one channel to another or if a fault or failure causes a change from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine shall not exceed any of its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18427]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17258]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a Fault or Failure results in a change from one Control Mode to another, or from one channel to another, or from the Primary System to the Back-up System, the Engine Control System shall maintain the engine within operating limits.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18428]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17259]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall provide the operator with the ability to shut down the engine rapidly.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18429]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17260]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall provide the operator with the ability to shut down the engine rapidly.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18430]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17261]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall shut down the Engine rapidly.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18431]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17262]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall provide a means for rapidly shutting down the Engine.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18432]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17263]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be able to shut down the engine rapidly.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18433]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17264]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The software and encoded logic shall be designed using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p><p>The software and encoded logic shall be implemented using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p><p>The software and encoded logic shall be verified using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18434]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17265]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The software and encoded logic shall be designed, implemented, and verified using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions to minimize errors.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18435]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17266]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>All associated software and encoded logic must be designed, implemented and verified to minimise the existence of errors by using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18436]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17267]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>All associated software and encoded logic shall be designed using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions to minimize errors.</p><p>All associated software and encoded logic shall be implemented using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions to minimize errors.</p><p>All associated software and encoded logic shall be verified using an approved method consistent with the criticality of the performed functions to minimize errors.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18437]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17268]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>All encoded logic shall use approved methods to minimise the existence of errors for implementation that are consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p><p>All associated software shall use approved methods to minimise the existence of errors for implementation that are consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p><p>All associated software shall use approved methods to minimise the existence of errors for verification that are consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p><p>All encoded logic shall use approved methods to minimise the existence of errors for verification that are consistent with the criticality of the performed functions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18438]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17269]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as the system complies with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall be able to complete a system safety assessment.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that result in a change in thrust or power.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that result in transmission of erroneous data.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that affect engine operability and their predicted frequency of occurrence.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18439]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17270]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>When the system complies with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that result in a change in thrust or power.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that result in transmission of erroneous data.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall identify faults or failures that affect engine operability.</p><p>The system safety assessment shall include the predicted frequency of occurrence of identified faults or failures.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18440]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17271]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>When complying with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, a system safety assessment must be completed for the Engine Control System. This assessment must identify Faults or Failures that result in a change in thrust or power, a transmission of erroneous data, or an effect on Engine operability together with the predicted frequency of occurrence of these Faults or Failures.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18441]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17272]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the Engine Control System complies with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall undergo a system safety assessment that identifies faults or failures resulting in a change in thrust or power, transmission of erroneous data, or effect on Engine operability, and the predicted frequency of occurrence of these faults or failures.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18442]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17273]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If complying with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment for faults or failures that result in a change in thrust or power.</p><p>If complying with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment for faults or failures that result in a transmission of erroneous data.</p><p>If complying with CS-E 210 or CS-E 510, the Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment for faults or failures that result in an effect on Engine operability.</p><p>As soon as the system safety assessment identifies faults or failures, the system safety assessment shall identify the predicted frequency of occurrence of these Faults or Failures.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18443]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17274]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System must be designed so that the loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System will not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18444]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17275]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed in a way that, if electrical power from the aircraft is lost or interrupted, no Hazardous Engine Effect occurs.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18445]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17276]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System is lost or interrupted, the system Engine Control System shall prevent a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18446]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17277]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed in a way that loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System does not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18447]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17278]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System lasts, the Engine Control System shall prevent a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18448]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17279]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof to perform the intended functions with adequate sensitivity and accuracy in modulating Engine power or thrust over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18449]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17280]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof to perform the intended functions with adequate sensitivity and accuracy in modulating Engine power or thrust over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18450]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17281]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which allows modulation of Engine power or thrust with adequate sensitivity and accuracy over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18451]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17282]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall modulate engine power or thrust with adequate sensitivity and accuracy over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</p><p>The Engine Control System's performance shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18452]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17283]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be able to modulate the Engine power or thrust with adequate sensitivity and accuracy over the declared range of Engine operating conditions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18453]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17284]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If an electronic over-speed protection system is provided, the system shall provide a means to test the protection function for availability.</p><p>The test means shall enable a complete test of the electronic over-speed protection system within the minimum number of cycles.</p><p>If the test is not fully automatic, the Engine instructions for operation shall contain the specification for a manual test.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18454]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17285]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If electronic over-speed protection systems are provided, the system shall include a means to test the protection function to establish availability A13:A15.</p><p>The test means shall enable a complete test of the system in the minimum number of cycles.</p><p>If the test is not fully automatic, the Engine instructions for operation shall contain the specification for manual testing.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18455]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17286]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>When electronic over-speed protection systems are provided, the design must include a means for testing the system to establish the A13:A15 availability of the protection function. The means must be such that a complete test of the system can be achieved in the minimum number of cycles. If the test is not fully automatic, the specification for a manual test must be contained in the Engine instructions for operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18456]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17287]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If electronic over-speed protection systems are provided, the system shall provide a means to test the A13:A15 availability of the protection function.</p><p>The number of cycles for a complete test of the protection function shall be minimal.</p><p>If the test is not fully automatic, the engine operation instructions shall specify the manual test procedure.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18457]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17288]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If electronic over-speed protection systems are provided, the Engine Control System shall be able to test the A13:A15 availability of the over-speed protection function.</p><p>The number of cycles of the over-speed protection availability test shall be minimal.</p><p>If the over-speed protection availability test is not fully automatic, the DOA shall provide the specification for a manual test in the Engine instructions for operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18458]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17289]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed in a way the loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System can be operated without causing the unacceptable transmission of erroneous data.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18459]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17290]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System is lost or interrupted, the Engine Control System shall prevent the transmission of erroneous data.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18460]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17291]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If aircraft electrical power supplied to the Engine Control System is lost or if aircraft electrical power supplied to the Engine Control System is interrupted, the Engine Control System shall inhibit the transmission of erroneous data.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18461]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17292]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System is lost or interrupted, the Engine Control System shall not transmit erroneous data.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18462]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17293]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as loss or interruption of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System lasts, the Engine Control System shall prevent the unacceptable transmission of erroneous data.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18463]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17294]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed and constructed to be essentially single fault tolerant for electrical and electronic failures with respect to LOTC\/LOPC events during Full-up Configuration.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18464]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17295]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be essentially single fault tolerant for electrical and electronic failures with respect to LOTC/LOPC events.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18465]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17296]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the Engine Control System is in the state Full-up Configuration, the fault tolerance of the Engine Control System with respect to electrical and electronic failures for LOTC/LOPC events shall be single-fault tolerant.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18466]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17297]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>In the Full-up Configuration, the fault tolerance of the Engine Control System for electrical and electronic failures during LOTC/LOPC events shall be single fault tolerant.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18467]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17298]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as in full-up configuration, the Engine Control System shall be essentially single Fault tolerant for electrical and electronic Failures with respect to LOTC/LOPC events.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18468]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17299]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a single failure occurs in the Aircraft-Supplied Data, the system shall not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect for any Engine.</p><p>The system shall ensure that loss of Aircraft-Supplied Data due to a single failure does not cause a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p><p>The system shall ensure that interruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data due to a single failure does not lead to a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p><p>The system shall ensure that corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data due to a single failure does not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18469]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17300]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a single failure leads to loss of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine system shall not exhibit a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p><p>If a single failure causes interruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine system shall not exhibit a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p><p>If a single failure leads to corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine system shall not exhibit a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18470]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17301]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a single failure leads to loss, interruption, or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine System shall prevent a Hazardous Engine Effect for any Engine.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18471]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17302]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a single failure leads to loss, interruption, or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the system shall not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect for any Engine.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18472]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17303]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall prevent a hazardous engine effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18473]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17304]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The electrical power requirements, including transient and steady state voltage limits, that are supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for starting and operating the Engine shall be identified and declared in the Engine instructions for installation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18474]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17305]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System shall include the need for power to be identified and documented in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The characteristics of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System, including transient and steady state voltage limits, shall be declared in the Engine instructions for installation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18475]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17306]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system Engine Installation Instructions shall identify the need for aircraft-supplied electrical power for the Engine Control System during start and run.</p><p>The system Engine Installation Manual shall specify aircraft-supplied power requirements for the Engine Control System during start and run.</p><p>The system Engine Installation Manual shall document the characteristics of aircraft-supplied electrical power for the Engine Control System during start and run, including transient and steady-state voltage limits.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18476]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17307]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine instructions for installation shall specify the electrical power supply characteristics from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for starting and operating the Engine, including transient and steady state voltage limits.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18477]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17308]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The DOA shall declare the need for any electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for starting the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The DOA shall declare the characteristics of any electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for starting the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The DOA shall declare the need for any electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for operating the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The DOA shall declare the characteristics of any electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for operating the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The DOA shall include transient voltage limits to the characteristics of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for operating the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p><p>The DOA shall include steady state voltage limits to the characteristics of electrical power supplied from the aircraft to the Engine Control System for operating the Engine in the Engine instructions for installation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18478]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17309]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, the over-speed function shall remain available between inspection and maintenance periods.</p><p>If over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, the availability of the over-speed function shall be demonstrated by test or other acceptable means.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18479]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17310]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, the over-speed function of the system shall remain available between inspection and maintenance periods and shall be demonstrated by test or other acceptable means.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18480]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17311]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, the availability of the over-speed function shall be demonstrated by test or other acceptable means between inspection and maintenance periods.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18481]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17312]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>When hydromechanical over-speed protection is provided, the over-speed function shall remain available between inspection and maintenance periods.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18482]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17313]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If over-speed protection is provided through hydromechanical means, the Engine Control System shall ensure the over-speed function is available between inspection and maintenance periods.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18483]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17314]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If an Engine dedicated power source is required for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1), the system shall provide sufficient capacity to account for Engine operation below idle.</p><p>The Engine Control System shall be designed and expected to recover Engine operation automatically during operation below idle.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18484]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17315]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If an Engine dedicated power source is required for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1), the capacity of the power source shall provide sufficient margin to account for Engine operation below idle.</p><p>As long as the Engine is operating below idle, the Engine Control System shall be designed and expected to recover Engine operation automatically.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18485]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17316]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The capacity of the Engine dedicated power source shall be sufficient to account for Engine operation below idle for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p><p>The capacity of the Engine dedicated power source shall be sufficient during automatic recovery of Engine operation by the Engine Control System for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18486]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17317]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If an Engine dedicated power source is required for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1), the capacity margin of the Engine dedicated power source shall be sufficient for Engine operation below idle in scenarios where the Engine Control System is designed to automatically recover Engine operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18487]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17318]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If an Engine dedicated power source is required for compliance with CS-E 50 (h)(1), the margin of the capacity of the dedicated power source shall be sufficient to maintain Engine operation below idle.</p><p>As soon as below idle, the Engine Control System shall recover Engine operation automatically.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18488]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17319]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The engine with a 30-Second OEI Power Rating shall incorporate means or provision for means for automatic availability and automatic control of the 30-Second OEI Power within its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18489]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17320]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>Engines having a 30-Second OEI Power Rating shall incorporate means or provision for means for automatic availability and automatic control of the 30-Second OEI Power within its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18490]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17321]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the Engine has a 30-second OEI power rating, the Engine shall automatically manage the 30-second OEI power within its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18491]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17322]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The engine shall automatically provide the 30-Second OEI Power within the engine's operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18492]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17323]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the engine has a 30-Second OEI Power Rating, the Engine Control System shall be able to automatically provide availability of the 30-Second OEI Power within its operating limitations.</p><p>If the engine has a 30-Second OEI Power Rating, the Engine Control System shall be able to automatically control the 30-Second OEI Power within its operating limitations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18493]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17324]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If low voltage transients are outside of the power supply voltage limitations declared under CS-E 50 (h)(3), the system shall meet the specifications of CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p><p>As soon as aircraft supplied electrical power returns to within the declared limits, the Engine Control System shall resume normal operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18494]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17325]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>Low voltage transients outside of the power supply voltage limitations declared under CS-E 50 (h)(3) shall meet the specifications of CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p><p>As soon as the aircraft supplied electrical power returns to within the declared limits, the Engine Control System shall resume normal operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18495]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17326]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the power supply voltage is outside the limitations declared under CS-E 50(h)(3), low-voltage transients shall meet the specifications of CS-E 50(h)(1).</p><p>As soon as the aircraft-supplied electrical power returns within the declared limits, the Engine Control System shall resume normal operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18496]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17327]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If low voltage transients cause the power supply voltage to fall outside the declared limits in CS-E 50 (h)(3), the Engine Control System shall comply with CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p><p>As soon as aircraft supplied electrical power returns to within the declared limits in CS-E 50 (h)(3), the Engine Control System shall resume normal operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18497]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17328]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as low voltage transients outside of the power supply voltage limitations as declared under CS-E 50 (h)(3) occur, the Engine Control System shall meet the specifications of CS-E 50 (h)(1).</p><p>As soon as aircraft supplied electrical power returns to within the declared limits, the Engine Control System shall resume normal operation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18498]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17329]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The performance of the intended functions by the Engine Control System shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof to ensure no unacceptable thrust or power oscillations are created.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18499]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17330]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>It shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions without creating unacceptable thrust or power oscillations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18500]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17331]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which does not create unacceptable thrust or power oscillations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18501]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17332]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall not create unacceptable thrust or power oscillations during intended functions, as verified through tests, analysis, or a combination thereof.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18502]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17333]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall not create unacceptable thrust or power oscillations.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18503]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17334]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the signal lines experience blockage, the system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) shall consider the effects on the Engine Control System.</p><p>If the signal lines experience leakage, the system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) shall consider the effects on the Engine Control System.</p><p>The system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) shall result in the adoption of appropriate design precautions for the Engine Control System.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18504]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17335]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be considered in the system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) for the effects of blockage or leakage of the signal lines.</p><p>Appropriate design precautions shall be adopted based on the system safety assessment of CS-E 50 (d) regarding blockage or leakage of the signal lines.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18505]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17336]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The scope of the system safety assessment in accordance with CS-E 50 (d) shall be inclusive of the effects of blockage and leakage of the signal lines on the Engine Control System.</p><p>The Engine Control System shall implement design precautions for blockage and leakage of the signal lines in accordance with CS-E 50 (d).</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18506]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17337]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The safety assessment for CS-E 50 (d) shall consider the effects of signal line blockage or leakage in the Engine Control System.</p><p>The design process shall adopt appropriate precautions for signal line blockage or leakage in the Engine Control System.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18507]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17338]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment for effects of blockage of the signal lines.</p><p>The Engine Control System shall complete a system safety assessment for effects of leakage of the signal lines.</p><p>The Engine Control System shall adopt appropriate design precautions to effects of blockage of the signal lines.</p><p>The Engine Control System shall adopt appropriate design precautions to effects of leakage of the signal lines.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18508]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17339]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed and constructed such that foreseeable failures or malfunctions leading to local events in the intended aircraft installation, such as fire, overheat, or failures leading to damage to Engine Control System components, do not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18509]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17340]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System must be designed and constructed so that foreseeable Failures or malfunctions leading to local events in the intended aircraft installation, such as fire, overheat, or Failures leading to damage to Engine Control System components, must not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect due to Engine Control System Failures or malfunctions.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18510]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17341]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the system Engine Control System experiences a foreseeable failure or malfunction, the system Engine Control System shall prevent Hazardous Engine Effects.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18511]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17342]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If foreseeable Failures or malfunctions lead to local events such as fire, overheat, or damage to Engine Control System components, the Engine Control System shall not cause Hazardous Engine Effects.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18512]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17343]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed in a way that, as soon as foreseeable Failures or malfunctions lead to local events in the intended aircraft installation or damage to Engine Control System components, the engine can be operated without a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18513]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17344]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall detect single failures leading to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data.</p><p>The system shall accommodate single failures leading to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data.</p><p>The accommodation strategy shall not result in an unacceptable change in thrust or power.</p><p>The accommodation strategy shall not result in an unacceptable change in Engine operating and starting characteristics.</p><p>The effects of single failures on Engine power or thrust shall be evaluated and documented throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>The effects of single failures on Engine operability and starting characteristics shall be evaluated and documented throughout the flight envelope.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18514]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17345]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption, or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the system shall detect and accommodate the failure.</p><p>The accommodation strategy shall not result in an unacceptable change in thrust or power.</p><p>The accommodation strategy shall not result in an unacceptable change in Engine operating and starting characteristics.</p><p>The effects of single failures on Engine power or thrust, Engine operability, and starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope shall be evaluated and documented.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18515]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17346]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>Single Failures leading to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, must be detected and accommodated. The accommodation strategy must not result in an unacceptable change in thrust or power or an unacceptable change in Engine operating and starting characteristics. The effects of these Failures on Engine power or thrust, Engine operability and starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope must be evaluated and documented. </p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18516]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17347]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system shall detect single failures leading to loss, interruption, or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data.</p><p>The system shall accommodate single failures leading to loss, interruption, or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data.</p><p>The system shall ensure that the accommodation strategy does not result in unacceptable changes to thrust, power, or engine operating and starting characteristics.</p><p>The system shall evaluate the effects of failures on engine power, thrust, operability, and starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>The system shall document the effects of failures on engine power, thrust, operability, and starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18517]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17348]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall detect the single failure.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall accommodate for the single failure.</p><p>Single failure accomodation of the Engine Control System shall prevent unacceptable change in thrust or power.</p><p>Single failure accommodation of the Engine Control System shall prevent unacceptable change in operating characteristics.</p><p>Single failure accommodation of the Engine Control System shall prevent unacceptable change in starting characteristics.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall evaluate the effects of these Failures on Engine power or thrust throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall evaluate the effects of these Failures on Engine operability characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall evaluate the effects of these Failures on Engine starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall document the effects of these Failures on Engine power or thrust throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall document the effects of these Failures on Engine operability characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p><p>As soon as a single failure leads to loss, interruption or corruption of Aircraft-Supplied Data, the Engine Control System shall document the effects of these Failures on Engine starting characteristics throughout the flight envelope.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18518]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17349]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed and constructed such that single failures of its components do not result in a hazardous engine effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18519]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17350]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be designed such that a single failure of any component does not result in a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18520]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17351]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If a single failure of an Engine Control System component occurs, the classification of the engine effect shall be not equal to Hazardous Engine Effect as specified by the higher-level safety goal.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18521]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17352]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The occurrence of Hazardous Engine Effects resulting from Single Failures of Engine Control System components shall be none.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18522]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17353]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As soon as Single Failures of Engine Control System components occurs, the Engine Control System shall prevent a Hazardous Engine Effect.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18523]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17354]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be substantiated by tests, analysis, or a combination thereof to perform the intended functions in a manner that maintains selected values of relevant control parameters.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18524]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17355]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall perform the intended functions in a manner that enables selected values of relevant control parameters to be maintained.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18525]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17356]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>It must be substantiated by tests, analysis or a combination thereof that the Engine Control System performs the intended functions in a manner which enables selected values of relevant control parameters to be maintained.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18526]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17357]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>Control Parameter Maintenance</p><p>Tests and analysis shall verify the Engine Control System's maintenance of selected values of relevant control parameters.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18527]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17358]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The Engine Control System shall be able to maintain selected values of relevant control parameters.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18528]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17359]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS should be able to determine the public holidays in Germany from January 01 2017 until December 31 2027 (at least).</p><p>The federal state must be configurable.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18529]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17360]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the time period is from January 01, 2017 until December 31, 2027, the system TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Germany.</p><p>The system TSS shall provide the user with the ability to configure the federal state of Germany.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18530]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17361]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system TSS should determine public holidays in Germany for any date from January 1, 2017 through December 31, 2027 at minimum.</p><p>The system TSS shall provide the user with the ability to configure the federal state for public holiday determination.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18531]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17362]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall determine public holidays in Germany from January 01, 2017 until December 31, 2027.</p><p>The TSS shall provide the user with the ability to configure the federal state.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18532]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17363]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS should be able to determine the public holidays in Germany from January 01 2017 until December 31 2027 (at least).</p><p>If the public holidays in Germany are determined, the TSS shall provide the user with the ability to configure the federal state.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18533]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17364]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the date is from January 01, 2017 to December 31, 2027, the TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18534]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17365]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the date is between January 01, 2017 and December 31, 2027, the TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18535]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17366]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>If the requested date is within the range from January 01 2017 to at least December 31 2027, the system TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18536]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17367]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall be able to determine public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate for at least the period from January 01, 2017 to December 31, 2027.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18537]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17368]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall be able to determine the public holidays in Rhineland-Palatinate starting from January 01 2017 until December 31 2027 (at least).</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18538]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17369]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet using the formula: hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek.</p><p>As long as the contract's TimesheetFrequency is set to weekly, the TSS shall calculate hours due for a week.</p><p>As long as the contract's TimesheetFrequency is set to monthly, the TSS shall calculate hours due for a month.</p><p>The TSS shall count only public holidays that occur on working days in the hours due calculation.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18539]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17370]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>As long as the TimesheetFrequency of the contract is weekly, the TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet using the formula: hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek.</p><p>As long as the TimesheetFrequency of the contract is monthly, the TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet using the formula: hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek.</p><p>Only public holidays that fall on working days shall be counted in the calculation of hoursDue.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18540]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17371]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The system TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet using the formula hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek.</p><p>The system TSS shall set the period of the Timesheet according to the TimesheetFreqeuency of the contract, where weekly corresponds to a week and monthly corresponds to a month.</p><p>The system TSS shall include public holidays only if they fall on working days when calculating hours due.</p><p>If workingDaysPerWeek equals 5, the system TSS shall classify the days of the week as follows: Monday to Friday as working days and Saturday and Sunday as non-working days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18541]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17372]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall determine the period for timesheet calculation as a week or a month based on the TimesheetFrequency of the contract.</p><p>The TSS shall calculate hoursDue as (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek, where publicHolidaysInPeriod is the count of public holidays falling on working days.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
            <row>
                <id><![CDATA[18542]]></id>
                <qid><![CDATA[17373]]></qid>
                <question><![CDATA[<p>The TSS shall calculate the hours due for a Timesheet by hoursDue = (workingDaysInPeriod - publicHolidaysInPeriod) * hoursPerWeek / workingDaysPerWeek.</p>]]></question>
                <help />
                <script />
                <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
            </row>
